The '''Northern Triangle''' ({{Langx|bl|Triángulo Norte}}; {{Langx|ca|Triangle Septentrional}}) is a geographical and cultural [[W:Peninsula|peninsular]] region of the [[W:Continent|continent]] of [[Abyala]]. Covering approximately {{Convert|5000000|km2|sqmi|abbr=on}} km², it is located entirely within the sovereign state of [[Balisca]]. The peninsula is bounded by the [[Salsipuedes Sea]] to the west, the [[Aethiopian Ocean]] to the north and east.

The term '''Baliscan Triangle''' ({{Langx|bl|Triángulo Baliscano}}) refers to the same region, but is used in a strictly [[W:Geopolitics|geopolitical]] sense, referencing the [[Cap de Pingüins|administrative control]] and military presence that Balisca exerts over far-flung insular territories in the region. Baliscan-controlled territories in the Triangle are the [[Boreal Islands]] in the [[Shendan Ocean]], the [[Baliscan Arktici|Baliscan Arktici Territory]], and the [[Cabu Verd|Cabu Berd]] archipelago in the [[Ethiopian Ocean]].

